        <div class="lane"><p class="eb"><i>02</i> Build time: heavy work done once, shipped as data</p>
          <div class="ln"><span class="nd">Land outlines<small>d3-geo + topojson</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd hi">Sample a 1.5° grid<small>6,552 land dots</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd">500 path runs<small>4.7 KB of path</small></span><span class="gap"></span><span class="nd">Old site URLs<small>crawled list</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd">504 redirects<small>in site config</small></span></div></div>
        <div class="lane"><p class="eb"><i>03</i> In the browser: scroll position drives everything that moves</p>
          <div class="ln"><span class="nd">Section in view<small>data-signal="flow"</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd">Signal store<small>one value, listeners</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd hi">Particle canvas<small>max 210 particles</small></span><span class="gap"></span><span class="nd">Scroll trigger<small>pin + scrub</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd">SVG diagram<small>strokes draw in</small></span></div></div>
        <div class="lane"><p class="eb"><i>04</i> Consent: a visitor's choice, recorded and cleaned up</p>
          <div class="ln"><span class="nd">Cookie banner<small>accept or reject</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd">First-party cookie<small>the decision</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd hi">Consent log<small>private store, no IP</small></span><span class="wr"></span><span class="nd">Nightly job<small>03:30, 12-month purge</small></span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="eng-notes">
      <div><h4>Publishing without rebuilding</h4><p>Every data request is labelled with the type of content it reads. When an editor publishes, the CMS calls a protected endpoint that clears only the pages carrying that label. Pages also refresh on their own every hour as a fallback.</p></div>
      <div><h4>A world map in 4.7 KB</h4><p>A script tests a grid of points against real coastlines once, then stores each row of land as a single line segment. The browser turns the 500 segments back into 6,552 dots using a dashed stroke, so the site ships no mapping library.</p></div>
      <div><h4>One simulation, six moods</h4><p>The background is a single canvas of at most 210 particles on springs. Sections only change its targets: where particles gather, how bright they are, how many connecting lines show. It pauses when the tab is hidden and draws one still frame for reduced-motion users.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Filters that live in the address</h4><p>The directory keeps its search, five filters and sort order in the URL. Option counts are recalculated against the other active filters on every change, which is what lets the page disable any option that would return nothing.</p></div>
